libdecor-cairo: vmlab: the title bar looks like GTK's Yaru-dark header bar, with full screen and hide buttons

For the Mac VM's window (mac26.sh), whose title bar this plugin draws: the same height, colours,
title font (VMLAB_DECOR_FONT, a Pango font name, in bold; VMLAB_DECOR_FONT_AA=rgba for subpixel
text), round buttons and icons (vmlab-icons.h, made by ../gen-icons.py from the desktop's icon
theme) as the Windows VM's GTK title bar, so the two windows match. One more button, left of
minimize, makes the window full screen. No title bar is drawn while the window is full screen.

With VMLAB_WINDOW_CONTROL (a FIFO the window reads "show" and "hide" lines from), a hide button
stands left of full screen; a click writes "hide" there, and the VM keeps running.

With VMLAB_SAVE_COMMAND (`vm save mac --button`), a save button stands left of hide; a click
runs that command (sh, without QEMU's files or signal settings) and the button shows how it
goes: a spinner while it runs, then a tick (exit 0) or an error mark (other than 3) for 4 s. A
thread of ours waits for the command and wakes the main loop with a compositor round trip; the
bar is drawn again in the plugin's dispatch, on the main thread.

The title bar is a desynchronized sub-surface, so a button's hover look shows at once: synced,
its redraws waited for the window's next commit, which reims makes only for a new guest frame,
and an idle Mac sends almost none (the buttons had no hover look).

Apply with patch -p1 in libdecor-0.2.2 (the tarball beside this file, unpacked).

